---
name: run
description: Run the `{{ name }}` command for the user ({{ description | replace('"', "'") | trim('.') }}). Use when the user asks for what {{ name }} does, or names it.
argument-hint: "[arguments of {{ name }}]"
---

<!-- First skill of the plugin, the counterpart of the example command: replace it with the
tool's real skills, one folder per verb (`skills/<verb>/SKILL.md`, `name` = the folder). -->

1. Find the command: `{{ name }}` when it is installed on the machine (`uv tool install
   --editable backend` in its repo), otherwise `uv run --project <its repo>/backend {{ name }}`.
2. Run `{{ name }} $ARGUMENTS`; when the arguments are unclear, read `{{ name }} --help` first
   rather than guessing an option.
3. Report what the command printed, and its exit code when it is not 0, without hiding an error.
